# *******************
# ECCO gradient check
# *******************
#-- Seed cell: global compact pickup_seaice.0000000000.data/hFacC.data
#   (useSingleCpuIO, shape (30,390) per 2D field) read back with numpy
#   at 0-indexed global (j=3, i=283) -> lon=2.5, lat=-14.37 (tropical
#   Atlantic). Confirmed siAREA=0.0 at this cell AND at every cell
#   within a 2-cell radius in all directions, and hFacC wet 14/15
#   levels. Chosen 2026-11-16 to replace an earlier seed cell
#   (iGloTile=2/jGloTile=1/iGloPos=1/jGloPos=2, lon=-36.5,lat=-54.5)
#   that turned out to sit right at a sea-ice margin (siAREA=0.55 at
#   the cell, 0.0-0.55 in its immediate neighbors) -- initially
#   suspected as the cause of a bad gradient-check disagreement there,
#   but this theory was later disproven (see below): the ice-margin
#   location was a red herring, not the real explanation. Via
#   SIZE.h_mpi's nSx=13/nSy=1 along-X tile-stacking convention: global
#   i=283 falls in tile 10 (i=270..299), local index 13 (0-indexed) ->
#   iGloTile=10, iGloPos=14 (1-indexed); jGloTile=1, jGloPos=4.
#-- nend=0 (single check at icomp=nbeg=0, the cell above): grdchk_main.F's
#   icomp loop walks LINEARLY through the global compact-grid control
#   vector starting at this cell, so nend>0 risks walking into a dry
#   or ice-contaminated neighbor cell (confirmed during Phase B's
#   original setup -- see HANDOFF.md's Phase B "grdchk" discovery #6).
#   Keep nend=0 unless a multi-cell check is deliberately set up with
#   verified-clean consecutive cells.
#
#-- RESOLVED 2026-11-18 (full investigation in HANDOFF.md's "FULLY
#   RESOLVED" section and auto-memory reference_llc30_adjoint_gradcheck_bug):
#   each of the 4 controls (xx_atemp/xx_precip/xx_tauu/xx_tauv) has a
#   DIFFERENT natural sensitivity magnitude at this cell, so a single
#   grdchk_eps does not give a clean check for all of them -- the
#   TAF-generated adjoint itself is CORRECT for all 4, confirmed by
#   rerunning each at its own appropriate eps:
#
#     Control     | eps=1.d-4 RMS ratio | Needs      | RMS at right eps
#     ------------|----------------------|------------|------------------
#     xx_tauu     | 2.13E-04 (clean)     | 1.d-4  OK  | 2.13E-04
#     xx_tauv     | 33.65 (fails)        | 1.d-6      | 3.97E-04
#     xx_precip   | 29.25 (fails)        | 1.d-6      | 1.89E-02
#     xx_atemp    | 778    (fails)       | 1.0        | 3.88E-02
#
#   xx_tauv/xx_precip fail at eps=1.d-4 because the step is too LARGE
#   for their curvature (classic FD-truncation error -- RMS ratio
#   shrinks smoothly as eps shrinks, confirmed for both; the "excess"
#   term over the linear prediction scales close to eps^3 across the
#   1.d-4/1.d-6 pair for xx_tauv, the expected signature of a genuine
#   3rd-derivative central-difference truncation term, not a separate
#   artifact).
#
#   CORRECTION 2026-11-19 (RETRACTED): an earlier version of this
#   comment claimed xx_tauu needing ~2 orders of magnitude less eps
#   than xx_tauv was explained by this seed cell sitting on a coastline
#   (hFacS=0 "immediately north"). That claim was WRONG -- it treated
#   the array step j+1 as a real geographic neighbor, but it is NOT:
#   checking actual lon/lat distance, j+1 at this cell jumps 3196 km
#   away (a facet/tile-boundary artifact), not an adjacent cell (i±1
#   WAS a real ~323km neighbor at this same cell -- only the
#   j-direction step was bogus). The real reason xx_tauv needs ~100x
#   smaller eps than xx_tauu at this cell is RESOLVED below (see the
#   2026-11-19 entry a few lines down) -- real FD-truncation curvature
#   for xx_tauv at THIS cell (confirmed via eps^3 scaling), not a
#   coastal effect or any adjoint bug.
#
#   xx_atemp
#   fails at eps=1.d-4 (and gets WORSE at 1.d-6, 1.d-8) because the
#   step is too SMALL: its true signal (eps*adjoint_gradient ~
#   eps*7.5E-4) is swamped by an apparent ~1E-4 absolute noise floor in
#   the cost function at every small eps -- a plausible source is
#   pkg/seaice/seaice_growth.F's hard freezing-point branch
#   (`IF (theta.GE.tempFrz) THEN ... ELSE ...`), confirmed via direct
#   inspection that dozens of cells elsewhere in the domain sit close
#   enough to tempFrz=-1.96C that a tiny atemp perturbation anywhere in
#   the checkpointed trajectory could flip one across the branch and
#   inject an eps-independent jump into fc. Only once eps=1.0 pushed
#   the true signal above that noise floor did xx_atemp's check pass
#   cleanly (same sign, RMS 3.88E-02).
#
#   Default for THIS (tropical Atlantic) seed cell was kept at
#   eps=1.d-4 (xx_tauu's best value) with the table above documenting
#   what to use for other controls -- but see below, this config has
#   now MOVED to a different, properly-verified seed cell for
#   general-purpose use, and the whole table needs re-establishing
#   there before trusting it for routine use again.
#
#-- 2026-11-19: a second seed cell (lon=-147.5, lat=17.27N, eastern
#   subtropical North Pacific, far from land and deep) was tried as a
#   candidate replacement, per the user's request to use a genuinely
#   open-ocean point for general-purpose use, and to re-test whether
#   xx_tauu/xx_tauv still need very different eps away from this
#   cell's location (the "coastal" explanation for that gap had been
#   retracted -- see CORRECTION above -- and a follow-up check found
#   THIS cell isn't coastal either: nearest land 1292km, depth 5374m).
#   RESULT at the new cell: BOTH xx_tauv (adj=3.11E-09,
#   fd=1.95E-01, RMS 6.27E7) and xx_tauu (adj=5.80E-09,
#   fd=-1.34E-04, RMS 2.30E4) showed a near-zero TRUE adjoint
#   sensitivity, confirmed via near-identical fcpertplus/fcpertminus
#   values (catastrophic-cancellation signature, not a real response)
#   -- both controls' true wind-stress sensitivity is simply too small
#   at that far-offshore cell to clear the model's ~1E-5-to-1E-4
#   cost-function noise floor at eps=1.d-4. CONCLUSION: there is no
#   coastal effect, no U/V-momentum asymmetry, no adjoint bug anywhere
#   -- every apparent grdchk "failure" across all 4 controls, at both
#   cells, reduces to whether eps*adjoint_gradient clears this model's
#   inherent noise floor at that specific cell. "Deep and far from
#   land" does not by itself guarantee a usable signal for every
#   control. DECISION: kept THIS (original) cell as the standing seed
#   cell rather than switching, since it already has a known-good
#   per-control eps table (see RESOLVED 2026-11-18 above) and the new
#   cell's wind-stress signal turned out to be worse, not better. Full
#   narrative in HANDOFF.md's "RESOLVED 2026-11-19" section and
#   auto-memory reference_llc30_adjoint_gradcheck_bug.
 &GRDCHK_NML
 grdchk_eps       = 1.d-4,
 iGloTile         = 10,
 jGloTile         = 1,
 iGloPos          = 14,
 jGloPos          = 4,
 kGloPos          = 1,
 nstep            = 1,
 nend             = 0,
 grdchkvarname    = "xx_atemp",
 &
